IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcimr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- my claim and what follows it: the deemed liability
-- acceptance day and the provisional payments day (regs 19, 21, 22); notice of remunerated work (reg 20, a regulative rule,
-- Act s 32); a later certificate of capacity (reg 21); declarations while I live outside WA (reg 29); custody (reg 30);
-- prescribed health services (reg 32, Act s 74); workplace rehabilitation (regs 37, 39); my employer's injury management
-- system (reg 74); return to work case conferences (reg 81); medical examinations (reg 88); permanent impairment
-- assessors' requirements (reg 92); and my election to keep the right to seek damages (regs 120, 121).
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker. Every question is one the worker asks ("By when must I ...?", "Can I be required to ...?",
-- "May I ...?"). Duties the regulations put on the insurer, the employer or an assessor are encoded for what they mean to
-- the worker. A judgment the text hands to someone else (reasonable hours) is asked as a fact.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING
-- (with a NOTHING-kind comment) where it does not answer.
--
-- Edition: compilation version 00-c0-00, current from 30 June 2026 (mrdoc 49606), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49606.txt.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 19 October 2026, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- my claim`

§§ `regs 19, 21(6), 22 -- the deemed liability acceptance day and the provisional payments day`

-- Reg 19: "the deemed liability acceptance day for a claim is the day after the period of 120 days beginning on the day on
-- which the insurer or self-insurer receives the claim." Reg 22: the provisional payments day for a claim on which a
-- deferred decision notice was given "is the day after the period of 28 days beginning on the day on which the insurer or
-- self-insurer receives the claim." Reg 21(6): where a claim is amended into an incapacity claim by a later certificate of
-- capacity (reg 21(4)) and a deferred decision notice is given on it, both days run instead from "the day on which the
-- claim is amended and taken to be an incapacity claim". 120 days beginning on day D end on D plus 119; the day after is
-- D plus 120 (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my claim` IS A DATE
      `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the periods begin` MEANS
    IF `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred`
    THEN `the day it was amended`
    ELSE `the day the insurer received my claim`

@export What is my claim's deemed liability acceptance day, before which the insurer must decide a deferred claim (regs 19, 21(6)(a); Act s 29)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer's insurer (or your self-insured employer) received your claim
      `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a later certificate of capacity turned your claim into a claim for time off work, and the insurer then gave you a deferred decision notice on it
      `the day it was amended` IS A DATE @desc The day that later certificate of capacity was given to the insurer (any day if not amended)
GIVETH A DATE
`my deemed liability acceptance day` MEANS
    `the date` 120 `days after` (`the day the periods begin` `the day the insurer received my claim` `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred` `the day it was amended`)

@export What is my claim's provisional payments day, from which my employer must pay me provisionally on a deferred claim (regs 22, 21(6)(b); Act s 36)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer's insurer (or your self-insured employer) received your claim
      `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a later certificate of capacity turned your claim into a claim for time off work, and the insurer then gave you a deferred decision notice on it
      `the day it was amended` IS A DATE @desc The day that later certificate of capacity was given to the insurer (any day if not amended)
GIVETH A DATE
`my provisional payments day` MEANS
    `the date` 28 `days after` (`the day the periods begin` `the day the insurer received my claim` `my claim was amended into an incapacity claim and deferred` `the day it was amended`)

§§ `reg 20 -- notice of remunerated work (Act s 32)`

-- The parties and acts of the regulative rule in this module.
DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF
    `the worker`

DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of remunerated work`

-- Act s 32(1): a worker who makes an incapacity claim "must give notice to the employer or the insurer ... of any
-- remunerated work that the worker does for any other employer after the claim is made" (penalty "a fine of $5 000");
-- (5): "Subsection (1) does not apply unless the insurer or self-insurer has complied with subsection (4)" (telling the
-- worker of the duty, reg 20(2), (3)). Reg 20(1)(b): the notice must "be provided to the employer or insurer within 7 days
-- beginning on whichever is the later of -- (i) the worker commencing the remunerated work; or (ii) the worker receiving
-- information from the insurer or self-insurer regarding the worker's obligation". Time 0 is that later day; 7 days
-- beginning on it end on day 6.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`reg 20 -- I must give notice of my remunerated work within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the worker`
    MUST `give notice of remunerated work`
    WITHIN 6
    LEST BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "notice of remunerated work not given within 7 days beginning on the later day (Act s 32(1), reg 20(1)(b))"

DECLARE `What became of my duty` IS ONE OF
    `the duty does not arise`
    `the duty was kept`
    `the duty was not kept`
    `the duty is still open`

-- Runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where
-- the notice was given, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, it asks whether giving it today
-- would still be in time. It takes no DEONTIC input from outside.
GIVEN `the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was given` IS A NUMBER
      `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of my duty`
`what became of the reg 20 duty, given` `the notice was given` `on` `the day it was given` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `the notice was given`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `reg 20 -- I must give notice of my remunerated work within 7 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day it was given`), (EVENT `the worker` `give notice of remunerated work` `the day it was given`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty was kept`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `reg 20 -- I must give notice of my remunerated work within 7 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `today`), (EVENT `the worker` `give notice of remunerated work` `today`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty is still open`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`

@export By when must I give notice of remunerated work I do for another employer after my incapacity claim (reg 20(1)(b); Act s 32)?
GIVEN `the day I started the work` IS A DATE @desc The day you started the paid work for another employer
      `the day the insurer told me of my duty` IS A DATE @desc The day you received information from the insurer (or self-insurer) about your duty to give this notice, for example in its liability decision notice
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give notice of remunerated work` MEANS
    `the date` 6 `days after` (`the later of` `the day I started the work` `and` `the day the insurer told me of my duty`)

@export Have I kept my duty to give notice of remunerated work in time (reg 20(1)(b); Act s 32(1), (5))?
GIVEN `the insurer has told me of my duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer (or self-insurer) has informed you of your duty to give notice of remunerated work
      `the day the insurer told me of my duty` IS A DATE @desc The day you received that information (any day if never)
      `the day I started the work` IS A DATE @desc The day you started the paid work for another employer
      `I have given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your employer or the insurer the notice
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of my duty`
`Have I given notice of remunerated work in time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the insurer has told me of my duty`)
    THEN `the duty does not arise`
    ELSE `what became of the reg 20 duty, given` `I have given the notice` `on` (`day` `the day I gave it`) `as of` (`day` `today`)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS `the later of` `the day I started the work` `and` `the day the insurer told me of my duty`
        GIVEN `a day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `day` `a day` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the start` `to` `a day`)

-- Reg 20(1)(a): the notice must "contain the following information -- (i) the day on which the worker commenced the
-- remunerated work; (ii) if applicable, the day on which the worker ceased the remunerated work; (iii) the job title and a
-- description of the remunerated work; (iv) the amount of remuneration received; (v) the name, address and contact details
-- of the person for whom the remunerated work is or was performed".
@export Does my notice of remunerated work contain everything the regulations require (reg 20(1)(a))?
GIVEN `it gives the day I started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives the day you started the work
      `I have stopped the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have stopped doing that work
      `it gives the day I stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives the day you stopped (answer either way if you have not stopped)
      `it gives the job title and a description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives the job title and a description of the work
      `it gives the amount I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives the amount of pay you received
      `it gives the name, address and contact details of the person I work for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives the name, address and contact details of the person you do or did the work for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my notice of remunerated work contain everything required` IF
        `it gives the day I started`
    AND ((NOT `I have stopped the work`) OR `it gives the day I stopped`)
    AND `it gives the job title and a description`
    AND `it gives the amount I was paid`
    AND `it gives the name, address and contact details of the person I work for`

§§ `reg 21 -- a later certificate of capacity`

DECLARE `Who gets my later certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer`
    `my employer`

-- Reg 21(2): "Within 7 days after a worker receives a subsequent certificate of capacity, the worker must give the
-- subsequent certificate of capacity to -- (a) if an insured employer has given the worker's claim to the insurer -- the
-- insurer; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply -- the employer." (4): the claim "is amended and taken to be an incapacity
-- claim on the day on which the subsequent certificate of capacity is given to the insurer or self-insurer."
@export Who must I give my later certificate of capacity to, if it says I cannot work (reg 21(2))?
GIVEN `my insured employer has given my claim to its insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is insured and has passed your claim on to its insurer
GIVETH A `Who gets my later certificate`
`Who must I give my later certificate of capacity to` MEANS
    IF `my insured employer has given my claim to its insurer`
    THEN `the insurer`
    ELSE `my employer`

@export By when must I pass on a later certificate of capacity that says I cannot work (reg 21(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the later certificate of capacity
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pass on my later certificate of capacity` MEANS `the date` 7 `days after` `the day I received the certificate`

§§ `regs 29, 30 -- living outside WA, and custody`

-- Act s 65(1), (2): a worker entitled to income compensation who does not reside in WA must give the insurer declarations
-- by the worker and a medical practitioner as to capacity for work, at intervals; payment can be suspended for failure.
-- Reg 29: "(a) within 3 months after the day on which the worker no longer resides in the State; and (b) if the worker
-- continues to receive payment of income compensation and not reside in the State -- within 3 months after the day on
-- which the required declarations were last provided."
@export By when must I give the insurer my next declarations of my capacity for work while I live outside WA (reg 29; Act s 65)?
GIVEN `the day I stopped living in WA` IS A DATE @desc The day after which you no longer resided in Western Australia
      `I have given declarations since then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already given the insurer the required declarations since you left
      `the day I last gave them` IS A DATE @desc The day you last gave them (any day if never)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give my next declarations` MEANS
    IF `I have given declarations since then`
    THEN `the date` 3 `months after` `the day I last gave them`
    ELSE `the date` 3 `months after` `the day I stopped living in WA`

-- Act s 66(2): income compensation "must be suspended for any period during which the worker is -- (a) in custody ...; or
-- (b) otherwise serving a term of imprisonment of a kind prescribed by the regulations." Reg 30(1): "a worker is serving a
-- term of imprisonment if the worker is a prisoner as defined in the Prisons Act 1981 section 3(1)." "Prisoner" is a
-- borrowed term, asked. When I am not a prisoner, s 66(2)(a) (custody) may still apply: NOTHING.
@export Am I serving a term of imprisonment that suspends my income compensation (reg 30(1); Act s 66(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I am a prisoner under the Prisons Act 1981` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a prisoner as the Prisons Act 1981 (WA) section 3(1) defines it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I serving a term of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `I am a prisoner under the Prisons Act 1981`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: custody under s 66(2)(a) of the Act)

§§ `reg 32 -- prescribed health services (Act ss 71, 74)`

DECLARE `Health service` IS ONE OF
    `Acupuncture`
    `Chiropractic`
    `Clinical psychology`
    `Counselling psychology`
    `Exercise program`
    `Mental health social work`
    `Occupational therapy`
    `Osteopathy`
    `Physiotherapy`
    `Psychology`
    `Speech pathology`
    `Another health service`

-- Reg 32: "a health service listed in column 1 of an item of the Table is a health service the expenses in respect of which
-- are medical and health expenses, and the provider eligibility requirement listed in column 2 of that item is the provider
-- eligibility requirement for that health service." Column 2 asks for registrations and accreditations (AHPRA general
-- registration, endorsements, Exercise and Sports Science Australia, the Australian Association of Social Workers, Speech
-- Pathology Australia): borrowed, asked as one fact. Act s 74(2): "An employer is not liable for compensation for medical
-- and health expenses for a medical and health service provided by a person if the person does not satisfy the provider
-- eligibility requirements". Another service may be a medical and health expense under the other paragraphs of s 71(1).
@export Can the cost of my treatment count as a medical and health expense, as a health service the regulations list (reg 32; Act ss 71(1)(h), 74)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Health service` @desc The kind of health service you received
      `my provider meets the reg 32 requirement for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who treated you holds the registration, endorsement or accreditation column 2 of the reg 32 Table requires for that service (for example general registration as a physiotherapist with AHPRA)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my treatment count as a medical and health expense` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `Another health service` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the other paragraphs of s 71(1) of the Act)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `my provider meets the reg 32 requirement for it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `regs 37, 39 -- workplace rehabilitation`

-- Reg 37(1): a request for a workplace rehabilitation service "may be made by -- (a) a worker; ..."; (2) "A worker may
-- choose which approved workplace rehabilitation provider is to provide the workplace rehabilitation service."; (3) an
-- insurer recommending one "must inform the worker that the worker may choose a different" one. The permission is to
-- choose among approved providers: for a provider that is not approved the text gives no answer.
@export May I choose which workplace rehabilitation provider helps me (reg 37(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the provider is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider you want is an approved workplace rehabilitation provider
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I choose my workplace rehabilitation provider` MEANS
    IF `the provider is approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit: reg 37(2) speaks only of approved providers)

-- Reg 39: "A workplace rehabilitation service must be terminated if -- (a) an injured worker can no longer undertake or
-- participate in workplace rehabilitation; or (b) an injured worker is participating in workplace rehabilitation with a
-- different provider; or (c) the goal or outcome identified by the provider ... has been attained; or (d) a settlement
-- agreement has been registered under Part 2 Division 12 of the Act; or (e) the workplace rehabilitation provider's approval
-- is suspended or cancelled; or (f) the injured worker and the employer agree that the services ... are no longer
-- required." When none holds the text does not say the service must go on: NOTHING.
@export Must my workplace rehabilitation service end (reg 39)?
GIVEN `I can no longer take part in workplace rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can no longer undertake or take part in workplace rehabilitation
      `I am doing workplace rehabilitation with a different provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now in workplace rehabilitation with another provider
      `the goal or outcome the provider set has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goal or outcome the provider identified for its services has been attained
      `a settlement agreement has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a settlement agreement for your claim has been registered
      `the provider's approval is suspended or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider's approval has been suspended or cancelled
      `my employer and I agree the services are no longer needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer agree the provider's services are no longer required
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my workplace rehabilitation service end` MEANS
    IF     `I can no longer take part in workplace rehabilitation`
        OR `I am doing workplace rehabilitation with a different provider`
        OR `the goal or outcome the provider set has been reached`
        OR `a settlement agreement has been registered`
        OR `the provider's approval is suspended or cancelled`
        OR `my employer and I agree the services are no longer needed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: reg 39 lists when the service must end, not when it must continue)

§§ `regs 74, 81, 88 -- injury management, case conferences and medical examinations`

-- Reg 74: "An employer must, on the request of a worker, provide the worker with a copy of the document that describes the
-- injury management system." "On the request" is read as a condition: without a request the duty does not arise.
@export Must my employer give me a copy of its injury management system document (reg 74)?
GIVEN `I have asked for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked your employer for a copy
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer give me its injury management system document` MEANS
    IF `I have asked for it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Reg 81: "(1) The maximum frequency a worker may be required to participate in a return to work case conference is not
-- more than once every 4 weeks. (2) Subregulation (1) does not apply if the return to work case conference is arranged by
-- the worker's treating medical practitioner. (3) A worker is not required to attend or participate in a return to work
-- case conference unless the conference is scheduled during reasonable hours." Once every 4 weeks: a conference at least
-- 28 days after the last one I was required to attend is within the limit (fork F6). Whether the hours are reasonable is a
-- judgment, asked. Within the limits, whether I am required at all is for s 165 of the Act, not encoded: NOTHING.
@export Can I be required to attend this return to work case conference (reg 81; Act s 165)?
GIVEN `it is scheduled during reasonable hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conference is scheduled during reasonable hours
      `my treating medical practitioner arranged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your treating doctor arranged this conference
      `I was required to attend an earlier conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been required to take part in an earlier return to work case conference
      `the day of the last one` IS A DATE @desc The day of the last case conference you were required to take part in (any day if none)
      `the day of this one` IS A DATE @desc The day of this conference
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be required to attend this case conference` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it is scheduled during reasonable hours`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     (NOT `my treating medical practitioner arranged it`)
              AND `I was required to attend an earlier conference`
              AND (`the days from` `the day of the last one` `to` `the day of this one`) LESS THAN 28
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 165 of the Act)

-- Reg 88: "(1) A worker must not be required under section 180 of the Act to undergo examination by a medical practitioner
-- -- (a) more frequently than once every 2 weeks; or (b) if the examination is scheduled during unreasonable hours. (2) A
-- worker must not be required under section 180 of the Act to attend medical examinations by more than 3 medical
-- practitioners who are specialists in the same field of medicine. (3) This regulation does not limit the number of times
-- a worker may be required to attend a medical examination by a medical practitioner." Once every 2 weeks: at least 14
-- days after the last (fork F6). Within the limits, s 180 of the Act decides: NOTHING.
@export Can I be required to attend this medical examination the employer has asked for (reg 88; Act s 180)?
GIVEN `it is scheduled during unreasonable hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examination is scheduled during unreasonable hours
      `I have had an earlier examination under s 180` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been required to undergo an examination under section 180 for this injury
      `the day of the last one` IS A DATE @desc The day of the last such examination (any day if none)
      `the day of this one` IS A DATE @desc The day of this examination
      `specialists in this field who have already examined me under s 180` IS A NUMBER @desc How many different specialists in the same field of medicine as this examiner you have already been required to see under section 180
      `this examiner is one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this examiner is one of those specialists already counted, or is not a specialist in that field
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be required to attend this medical examination` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is scheduled during unreasonable hours` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `I have had an earlier examination under s 180`
              AND (`the days from` `the day of the last one` `to` `the day of this one`) LESS THAN 14
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     (NOT `this examiner is one of them`)
              AND `specialists in this field who have already examined me under s 180` AT LEAST 3
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 180 of the Act)

§§ `reg 92 -- an approved permanent impairment assessor's requirements`

-- Reg 91: an assessor may require me to attend a place, to produce documents or information, or to consent to another
-- person producing them, by notice in the approved form. Reg 92: "If the time to comply with a requirement referred to in
-- regulation 91 is not specified, the requirement must be complied with within 7 days after the day on which the person
-- receives notice of the requirement." Where the notice specifies a time, that time governs and it is not in the text:
-- NOTHING.
@export By when must I comply with a requirement of an approved permanent impairment assessor (regs 91, 92)?
GIVEN `the notice specifies a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor's notice states the time by which you must comply
      `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the notice of the requirement
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I comply with the assessor's requirement` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies a time`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the time the notice specifies)
    ELSE JUST (`the date` 7 `days after` `the day I received the notice`)

§§ `regs 120, 121 -- my election to keep the right to seek damages (Act s 421)`

-- Reg 120(1): "a worker may elect to retain the right to seek an award of damages by completing the approved form and
-- lodging it with the Director." (2) It "must be accompanied by -- (a) the supporting assessment of the worker's degree of
-- permanent whole of person impairment ...; or (b) if the election ... is in respect of a dust disease -- (i) a supporting
-- assessment ... in the determination made by the Dust Disease Medical Panel under section 127 or 426(3) of the Act; or (ii)
-- an agreement made under section 426(5) of the Act". Whether the impairment reaches the s 421 threshold is for the Act
-- (encoded in the Act's own baseline), not this question.
@export Is my election to keep the right to seek damages made the way the regulations require (reg 120)?
GIVEN `I completed the approved form and lodged it with the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you completed the approved election form and lodged it with the Director of WorkCover WA's conciliation and arbitration services
      `my election is about a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the election concerns a dust disease
      `a supporting assessment of my whole of person impairment went with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supporting assessment of your degree of permanent whole of person impairment (in the approved form) went with the election
      `the Dust Disease Medical Panel's determination went with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dust disease: whether a supporting assessment in the Dust Disease Medical Panel's determination under s 127 or s 426(3) went with it
      `a s 426(5) agreement with my employer went with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dust disease: whether an agreement with your employer under s 426(5) stating your degree of impairment went with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election made the way the regulations require` IF
        `I completed the approved form and lodged it with the Director`
    AND (    ((NOT `my election is about a dust disease`) AND `a supporting assessment of my whole of person impairment went with it`)
         OR  (    `my election is about a dust disease`
              AND (`the Dust Disease Medical Panel's determination went with it` OR `a s 426(5) agreement with my employer went with it`)))
